  "design": "The limb implements the CommonMark 0.30 §4.5 fenced-code-block state machine in a single awk pass. Opener: up to 3 leading spaces then a run of >=3 identical backtick or tilde; for a backtick fence the info string may not contain a backtick (a tilde fence's info string may contain anything). Closer: up to 3 leading spaces, a run of the SAME marker character at least as long as the opener's run, and nothing but spaces/tabs after it. A different marker character never closes an open fence, and a shorter run of the same marker is content, not a closer. Every line of a fenced block, INCLUDING the opening and closing delimiter lines, is reported INSIDE, so a correction written onto a fence delimiter cannot satisfy a line-anchored limb. An unclosed fence extends to EOF: remaining lines are INSIDE and EOF state is OPEN (fail-closed, never silently closed). Every public function is a pure function of the file bytes; no global state is written. Sourcing defines functions only and runs nothing; a standalone CLI (--selftest/--report/--outside/--eof) sits behind the same BASH_SOURCE guard the round-40 suite uses. Public API: fence_scan, fence_report, fence_outside_lines, fence_outside_set, fence_outside_count, fence_outside_match FILE ERE, fence_eof_state, fence_line_state FILE N, fence_audit, fence_payload FILE ERE, fence_selftest. The ERE is matched against the whole line; callers anchor it themselves, e.g. ^Correction [(]round 41[)] (bracket form, not escaped parens, so it survives both shell and awk quoting).",
  "why_this_exists": "The round-40 scanner (corpus/instruments/r40-closure.sh lines 581-621, h2_scan) opens a fence on /^ {0,3}```/ but closes only on /^ {0,3}```[ \\t]*$/ — three backticks exactly. A CommonMark four-backtick fence therefore never closes, which is why round-40 wave-2 defeat fixture T3 read rc=1 payload=corrections=3,named=3,missing=1,fences=open on a well-formed file. The r40 scanner also had no notion of fence length (a ```` fence was indistinguishable from a ``` fence) and no notion of marker identity (tilde and backtick fences were the same state).",
