    "selftest": "7 graded cases, all pass, rc=0: A 4-backtick correction fenced; B T3 shape counts 3; C fenced M39-2 row; D well-formed CLOSED at EOF; E tilde fence honoured and a different marker does not close a fence; F unclosed fence reports OPEN; G a shorter run of the same marker does not close a longer fence.",
    "differential_crosscheck": "The INSIDE set was compared line-for-line against the CommonMark reference parser (python commonmark 0.9.2, CommonMark 0.29 reference implementation) on 27 fixtures covering 3- and 4-backtick fences, tilde fences, mixed markers, differing fence lengths, info strings containing a backtick, closers with trailing text, unclosed fences, fences at EOF, and indented fences: differential cases=27 diffs=0, rc=0. The reference HTML output was used to confirm the ambiguous closer-with-text case; the reference implementation was also checked against the cmark C binary from the same package for that case, with identical HTML.",
    "baseline": "On the same fixtures the round-40 scanner still reports h2_scan -> '0 0 open' for a-fourbacktick-correction.md and b-t3-style.md (it cannot close a 4-backtick fence at all), versus eof=CLOSED from the new limb.",
    "self_application": "The limb was run against this very receipt and found a real CommonMark error in it: proof (a) quoted the fixture (which contains a four-backtick fence) inside a four-backtick display fence, so the inner fence closed the outer one and EOF was left OPEN. The display fence was widened to five backticks. After the fix: outside=253 inside=145 eof=CLOSED, 10 fences / 10 closers. The limb caught a defect in its own author's document, which is the strongest available evidence it is not a rubber stamp.",
    "lane_corpus": "The limb was run over the lane's own files (read-only): SCORECARD.md 1600 lines outside=1547 inside=53 eof=CLOSED; LOG.md 1734 outside=1734 inside=0; SHONEN.md 219 outside=219 inside=0; PROVINCE.md 161 outside=117 inside=44; SKILL.md 1122 outside=1104 inside=18; corpus/README.md 543 outside=513 inside=30; corpus/SOURCES.md 135 outside=135 inside=0. All eof=CLOSED. corr41=count=0 everywhere is expected and correct: the Correction (round 41) blocks do not exist in the lane yet (owned by sibling seats ExecI1Blocks / ScribeCorrections); when they land this limb decides whether each correction line is fenced.",
    "robustness": "Runs clean under set -uo pipefail (the lane's suite setting). Missing file -> rc 1, no output, no crash. fence_selftest writes fixtures under $TMPDIR and removes them on exit; verified no leftover. Pure POSIX-ish awk (ENVIRON, substr, index, length, POSIX character classes only), no GNU-awk-only constructs. The transcript reproduces byte-identically from the delivered limb and scratch fixtures apart from its own utc= line, verified by re-running the driver (diff reports exactly one differing line, the timestamp)."
  },
